d>2025-08-09T00:16:13+05:30</updated> <id>https://prakassec.github.io//posts/Emotet/</id> <content src="https://prakassec.github.io//posts/Emotet/" /> <author> <name>Prakash Kumar</name> </author> <category term="SOC" /> <category term="Malware" /> <summary> Emotet is a sophisticated malware strain and cybercrime operation, first detected in 2014. Initially a banking Trojan, it evolved into a highly modular loader and botnet, delivering other malware like TrickBot, QBot, Ryuk, and IcedID, and often used in ransomware campaigns. </summary> </entry> <entry><title>Really Simple Security? More like Really Simple Hacking!(CVE-2024-10924)</title><link href="https://prakassec.github.io//posts/CVE-2024-10924/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Really Simple Security? More like Really Simple Hacking!(CVE-2024-10924)" /><published>2024-11-20T05:35:00+05:30</published> <updated>2024-11-20T11:58:57+05:30</updated> <id>https://prakassec.github.io//posts/CVE-2024-10924/</id> <content src="https://prakassec.github.io//posts/CVE-2024-10924/" /> <author> <name>Prakash Kumar</name> </author> <category term="VAPT" /> <category term="CVE" /> <summary> CVE-2024-10924 Really Simple Security WordPress plugin, affecting versions 9.0.0 to 9.1.1.1. The flaw enables attackers to bypass authentication, potentially gaining admin access to sites if the plugin’s two-factor authentication is enabled. What is Really Simple Security The Really Simple Security plugin formerly known as “Really Simple SSL,” is a popular WordPress plugin used to enhance ... </summary> </entry> <entry><title>Azure Powershell</title><link href="https://prakassec.github.io//posts/Azure-Powershell/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Azure Powershell" /><published>2024-11-10T15:27:00+05:30</published> <updated>2024-11-10T15:38:11+05:30</updated> <id>https://prakassec.github.io//posts/Azure-Powershell/</id> <content src="https://prakassec.github.io//posts/Azure-Powershell/" /> <author> <name>Prakash Kumar</name> <